cards.explanation:
A continuous-time process $W$ is a standard Brownian motion (Wiener process) if
- $W(0)=0$ and its paths are continuous;
- increments over non-overlapping intervals are independent;
- $W(t)-W(s)\sim N(0,\,t-s)$ for $s<t$.
Consequences: $W(t)\sim N(0,t)$, $E[W(t)]=0$, $E[W(t)^2]=t$, $\operatorname{cov}(W(s),W(t))=\min(s,t)$, and $W$ is both a martingale and a Markov process.
